16. My first novel, Sealed (2017), is a work of eco-horror, which was shortlisted for the Not the Booker Award 2018. My second novel, Exit Management (2020), moves between contemporary ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/naomi-r-booth/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sleeping on Jupiter won the DSC Prize for Fiction 2016 and was longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2015. All the Lives We Never Lived won the Sahitya Akademi, one of India's highest literary honours, and was shortlisted for the International Dublin Literary Award. It won Tata ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... shortlisted for the Royal Society of Literature Ondaatje Prize and the Women's Prize for Fiction\\n* Swing Time: longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2017\\n* Granta′s Best of Young British Novelists, 2003 and 2013\\n* 2016: Welt-Literaturpreis\\n* 2017: Langston Hughes Medal\\\"Zadie Smith Wins CCNY's Langston ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zadie_Smith\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... David Cohen Prize for Literature\\n*2011: Man Booker Prize, winner, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2011 Costa Book Awards, shortlist, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2012: Europese Literatuurprijs\\n*2015: Zinklar Award at the first annual Blixen Ceremony in Copenhagen\\n*2016: Siegfried Lenz Prize\\n*2017: Officier in the Ordre ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Barnes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was also shortlisted for the 2018 Saroyan Prize and longlisted for the 2018 PEN/Robert Bingham Prize for Debut Fiction and the 2017 Story Prize. Her novel The Gone Dead was published by Ecco/HarperCollins in June 2019 and was a New York Times Book Review Editor ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"80f3f7592272db6d55f5064b434744ea0617b9d276d60b57c48e201f47ecc048\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d039205ff8b874b00f36b3ad050362962f43ed3f305c7d9daad5e8465a05ee6c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... In London, Geetanjali Shree and Daisy Rockwell Win the 2022 International Booker Prize\\nauthor: Porter Anderson\\ndate: 2022-05-26\\n---\\n'Tomb of Sand' is the first novel translated from an Indian language to win the award. Shree and Rockwell split the International Booker's £50,000 purse.\\n\\nBy ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2024 Booker International Prize Winner:\\n\\nKairos by Jenny Erpenbeck translated by Michael Hofmann\\n\\n2024 Booker International Prize Shortlist finalists:\\n\\n-\\n\\nNot a River by Selva Almada\\n\\n-\\n\\nMater 2-10 by Hwang Sok-yong\\n\\n-\\n\\nWhat I'd Rather Not Think About by Jente Posthuma\\n\\n-\\n\\nCrooked Plow by Itamar Vieira Junior ... \",\"title\":\"https://bookclubs.com/blog/2023-2024-book-awards-and-book-prize-winners\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... fifth novel, Swimming Home, no one took it. That it was ever even published – earning the first of her two Booker shortlistings, in 2012 – owed to the disillusionment of former Amazon employee Stefan Tobler, now 49, then working as a freelance translator assessing potential foreign-language acquisitions for ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2019\\n\\nNo major changes for the press, but another good year for prize attention. Amy Arnold's Slip of a Fish landed a 2019 Goldsmiths Prize shortlisting, while Alia Trabucco Zerán's The Remainder was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize. Multiple translation prize wins and shortlistings ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize is awarded every year for a book that is translated into English and published in the UK or Ireland.\\n\\nShree's novel competed against five other shortlisted titles, by Mieko Kawakami, Bora Chung, Jon Fosse, Claudia Pineiro and former winner Olga Tokarczuk.\\n\\nBorn in ... \",\"title\":\"https://literaturecurry.com/news-details/1159/geetanjali-shree-is-first-indian-to-win-inter\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2025-01-01\\n---\\nDaniel Bowles longlisted for International Booker Prize\\n\\nThe English-language version of Christian Kracht's novel Eurotrash—translated from its original German by Associate Professor of German Studies Daniel Bowles—has been longlisted for the 2025 International Booker Prize. The annual prize, split equally between ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/sites/bc-news/articles/2025/spring/bc-professor-longlisted-for-international-booker-prize.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... Siegfried Lenz Prize\\n*2017: Officier in the Ordre National de la Légion d'Honneur\\n*2021: Jerusalem Prize\\n*2021: Yasnaya Polyana Prize (for Nothing to Be Frightened Of)\\n\\nList of works\\n\\nNovels\\n\\n* Metroland (1980)\\n* Before She Met Me (1982)\\n* Flaubert's Parrot (1984) – shortlisted for the Booker Prize\\n* Staring ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Barnes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... The 2022 International Booker Prize Shortlist\\nauthor: Geetanjali Shree; Daisy Rockwell\\ndate: 2022-06-24\\n---\\nThe International Booker Prize celebrates the best fiction in translation published over the previous year. Frank Wynne, acclaimed translator and chair of the 2022 judging panel, tells Five Books about the six novels ... \",\"title\":\"https://fivebooks.com/best-books/the-best-of-world-literature-the-2022-international-booker-prize-shortlist-frank-wynne/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"a511766f61b7642b2e523408a1b19b9c969e5cb291e65d60b93ec6adfb5c7945\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"7a842fff5a936d69bc85394208df25c2b7e964f3a9c583c899fd2f4df828b921\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated 26 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_755ddd3395af4217b2aebb14"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 with her breakthrough novel, The Vegetarian, translated by ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her best known novel, The Vegetarian (published in Korea in 2007), was her first to be translated into English, in 2015. It won the Man Booker International Prize in 2016, with the prize split between Han Kang and her translator, Deborah Smith.\\n\\nAt the time, Smith's translation ... \",\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... the International Booker prize in 2016—The White Book, Human Acts, and Greek Lessons. Kang, 53, has been a writer for over 30 years, but The Vegetarian was her first novel to be translated into English in 2015, and led to widespread acclaim and attention.\\n\\n\\\"Han Kang writes ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/7065011/nobel-prize-2024-winners/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... the translator who won the 2016 Man Booker International Prize for her translation of The Vegetarian by Korean author Han Kang\\n\\nIt's of particular importance to note that the winning International Booker Prize comes from an independent press.\\n\\nIn a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... Deborah Smith, Korean to English: 'Han Kang is very generous… she calls them \\\"our\\\" books'\\n\\nDeborah Smith is translator of The Vegetarian by the Korean writer Han Kang; she and Kang are the co-winners of the Man Booker International prize 2016. She is also the translator of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/jul/24/subtle-art-of-translating-foreign-fiction-ferrante-knausgaard\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... that confronts historical traumas and exposes the fragility of human life'.\\n\\nHan is the author of five books that have appeared in English: The Vegetarian (2016, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello)—which won the International Booker Prize, Human Acts (2017, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello), The White Book ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.booksandpublishing.com.au/articles/2024/10/14/260359/han-kang-wins-2024-nobel-prize-for-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... International Booker Prize\\n\\nFocusing on contemporary fiction originally written in English and published outside the UK and Ireland, this award champions exceptional storytelling from around the globe. Previous winners include Marlon James for \\\"A Brief History of Seven Killings\\\" and Han Kang for \\\"The Vegetarian,\\\" showcasing new and ... \",\"title\":\"https://inkerspress.com/top-10-most-prestigious-international-literary-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... before its nomination to 25,000 copies in the nine months after its win. (Not bad for a 624-page epic about a woman who won't get out of bed.) And the first winner, Han Kang's The Vegetarian in 2016, translated by Deborah Smith, about a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Deborah Smith is the Man Booker International Prize–winning translator of The Vegetarian by Han Kang and other books.\\n\\nHarmless Like You by Rowan Hisayo Buchanan\\n\\nRowan Hisayo Buchanan is a British-Japanese-Chinese-American novelist. She received a BA from Columbia University in New York, and currently ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... And for those of us interested in reading books that originate beyond the English-speaking world, they don't come much more major than the Man Booker International Prize, which was awarded for the first time last year to Han Kang and translator Deborah Smith for The Vegetarian ... \",\"title\":\"https://ayearofreadingtheworld.com/2017/04/29/book-of-the-month-samanta-schweblin/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6171a0fbd802450198af5a16edb840e9fabbc3e24aa290708c4baa9637428af4\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"35ad8d8683c7af0835aecd4b3c162302da61d81966065c1871c75280a3db66f3\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Han Kang Vegetarians translated 25 languages Booker International\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker International prize 2015 won by 'visionary' László Krasznahorkai\\nauthor: Alison Flood\\ndate: 2015-05-19\\n---\\nThe Hungarian author László Krasznahorkai, whose sentences roll out over paragraphs in what his translator George Szirtes has called a \\\"slow lava flow of narrative, a vast black river of type ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2015/may/19/man-international-booker-2015-laszlo-krasznahorkai\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... FINALISTS FOR TRANSLATED LITERATURE:\\n\\n- Khaled Khalifa, Death Is Hard Work\\n\\nTranslated from the Arabic by Leri Price\\n\\nFarrar, Straus and Giroux / Macmillan Publishers - László Krasznahorkai, Baron Wenckheim's Homecoming\\n\\nTranslated from the Hungarian by Ottilie Mulzet\\n\\nNew Directions - Scholastique Mukasonga, The Barefoot Woman\\n\\nTranslated from the French by ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/the-2019-national-book-awards-finalists-announced/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, the Polish novelist was recognized for \\\"Flights,\\\" which she calls a \\\"constellation novel,\\\" owing to its fragmentary form and genre-defying style, and which won that year's Man Booker Prize. \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead,\\\" her latest novel to be translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... He has translated many Hungarian writers including Imre Madách, Sándor Márai and László Krasznahorkai (winner of the 2015 Man Booker International). He won the Dery prize for his translation of Madách's The Tragedy of Man and the European Poetry Translation prize for Rakovsky's New Life.\\n\\nOf ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/jul/24/subtle-art-of-translating-foreign-fiction-ferrante-knausgaard\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... Broom accepts the 2019 National Book Award for Nonfiction for The Yellow House\\n\\nArthur Sze accepts the 2019 National Book Award for Poetry for Sight Lines\\n\\nLászló Krasznahorkai accepts 2019 National Book Award for Translated Literature\\n\\nEdmund White receives the 2019 Medal for Distinguished Contribution to American Letters ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/awards-prizes/national-book-awards-2019/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Studies in the Meaning of Poetry (collected essays including \\\"The Intentional Fallacy\\\" and \\\"The Affective Fallacy\\\", cowritten with Monroe Beardsley)\\n*Barbara Woodhouse\\n**Dog Training my Way\\n**Talking to Animals (autobiography)\\n\\nBirths\\n\\n*January 5 – László Krasznahorkai, Hungarian novelist and screenwriter\\n*January 15 – Jose Dalisay, Jr., Filipino writer\\n*January 29 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1954_in_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... SandlerNational Book Award for Translated Literature:\\n\\nBaron Wenckheim's Homecoming by László Krasznahorkai (author), Ottilie Mulzet (translator) -\\n\\n2018\\n\\nNational Book Award for Nonfiction:\\n\\nThe New Negro by Jeffrey C. StewartNational Book Award for Autobiography:\\n\\nBelonging by Nora KrugNational Book Award for Poetry:\\n\\nIndecency by Justin Phillip ReedNational Book ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bookbrowse.com/awards/detail/index.cfm/book_award_number/6/national-book-awards\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d79\"},\"ref\":\"d79\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Last Wolf by Laszlo Krasznahorkai, translated by John Batki & George Szirtes\\n\\nThe Last Wolf, told in a single very long sentence, flows from the mouth of a bereft narrator in a Berlin bar as he tries to explain to the bartender what happened when he was sent ... \",\"title\":\"https://electricliterature.com/9-novels-for-readers-interested-in-animal-perspectives/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... Carlo Emilio Gadda, Youssef Habchi El-Achkar, Franz Kafka, Søren Kierkegaard, Danilo Kiš, László Krasznahorkai, Richard Middleton, Kenji Miyazawa, Giuseppe Pontiggia, A. L. Snijders, Enrique Vila-Matas Translations: Nadeem Aslam, Tash Aw, John Banville, Frédéric Beigbeder, Laurent Binet, A. S. Byatt, Orly Castel-Bloom, J. M. Coetzee, Lydia ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timothy_McSweeney%27s_Quarterly_Concern\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... translated by Angela Roda (Weidenfeld & Nicolson); ROMBO by Esther Kinsky translated by Caroline Schmidt (Fitzcarraldo Editions); QUAND TU ECOUTERA CETTE CHANSON by Lola Lafon (Stock); A MOUNTAIN TO THE NORTH, A LAKE TO SOUTH, PATHS TO THE WEST, A RIVER TO THE EAST by László Krasznahorkai translated by ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.thewhitereview.org/feature/books-of-the-year-2023/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"3e1eabb95d8106b3cedec90193822ef0b29e4ddbe6a4f0f92fcac5cc6590dffe\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"915a01263db3d9da031649101790ba445ba0fe770d37065dfdd4f64965ad28cb\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"László Krasznahorkai Booker International Prize 2015 translated languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... Barksdale commented, \\\"In the past, the Man Booker International Prize–winner Ismail Kadare and Neustadt International Prize–winner Nurrudin Farah have also been mentioned as being on the shortlist of candidates for the Nobel Prize in Literature. The Nobel Prize awarded to Mo Yan was a validation of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.independentpublisher.com/article.php?page=1885\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... a Krasznahorkai story.\\\"\\n\\nThe biennial Man Booker International is worth £60,000, and is intended to honour a living author for their body of work, either written in English or available in English translation. It has gone in the past to Ismail Kadare from Albania, Chinua Achebe from ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2015/may/19/man-international-booker-2015-laszlo-krasznahorkai\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ismail Kadare – A winner of the Booker prize who fled Albania in 1990 for political reasons.\\n\\nShaparak \\\"Shappi\\\" Khorsandi – A British comedian and author of Iranian origin. She is the daughter of the Iranian political satirist and poet Hadi Khorsandi. Her family left Iran when she was a ... \",\"title\":\"https://refugeeweek.org.uk/resources/facts-figures-and-contributions/famous-refugees/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d84\"},\"ref\":\"d84\",\"snippet\":\" ... a large and growing international academic literature. Her famous works include La Place (\\\"A Man's Place\\\", 1983), L'événement (\\\"Happening\\\", 2000), Se perdre (\\\"Getting Lost\\\", 2001), L'Occupation (\\\"The Possession\\\", 2002), and Les Années (\\\"The Years\\\", 2008).Annie Ernaux annie-ernaux.org\\n\\nPrize announcement\\n\\nFollowing the announcement ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Nobel_Prize_in_Literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Winner of the 2019 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nRequest Book | Request E-Book | Request Audiobook\\n\\nAccessible editions: BK\\n\\nSet in Iran in the decade following the 1979 Revolution, this moving, richly imagined novel is narrated by the ghost of Bahar, a 13-year-old girl whose family is ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d85\"},\"ref\":\"d85\",\"snippet\":\" ... There are also two other Nobel Prize winners in chemistry: Lavoslav Ružićka and Vladimir Prelog. It's true that Ivo Andrić is the only winner of Nobel Prize in literature, but then you have to write like that…\\n\\nCan you please change that fact, as other readers will ... \",\"title\":\"https://blog.ed.ted.com/2016/12/08/the-worlds-required-reading-list-the-books-that-students-read-in-28-countries/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... As you'd expect from a Man Booker Prize-winner, Ishiguro delivered the goods, his understated prose telling the story of Mr. Stevens, a man so dedicated to the art of service (he's a butler, the majority of his career for Lord Darlington) he [spoiler alert!] fails ... \",\"title\":\"https://theconflictedfilmsnob.com/2017/10/23/kazuo-ishiguro-the-nobel-prize-winning-authors-film-adaptations/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... Burkandt, soruları cevapladıkça, bu konu bu kadar \\\"popüler\\\" olduğu için değil, gerçekten gezegenimiz ve insanlık için endişelendiğini ve bu konuda ne kadar samimi olduğunu anlıyoruz. Sorumluluklarının, hatalarının ve yapabileceklerinin farkında. Tüm bunlar da emin adımlarda ilerlediği kariyer yolculuğunda onu neden ilgi ve dikkatle izlememiz gerektiğini bir kere daha ... \",\"title\":\"https://vogue.com.tr/sosyal-etki/soyleyecek-sozu-cok-gloria-sophie-burkandt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... agree with all of this. (except that i\\n\\n- iceland\\n\\n- india\\n\\n- information\\n\\n- information flow\\n\\n- internet\\n\\n- interns\\n\\n- interview memes\\n\\n- iran\\n\\n- iraq\\n\\n- ireland\\n\\n- irish\\n\\n- irish sf\\n\\n- islam\\n\\n- israel\\n\\n- italy\\n\\n- james ii\\n\\n- james tait black prize winner\\n\\n- japan\\n\\n- jfk\\n\\n- jfk assassination\\n\\n- job hunt\\n\\n- jobs\\n\\n- jokes\\n\\n- jon ziegler goes into it thoroughly.\\n\\n- journalism ... \",\"title\":\"https://nwhyte.livejournal.com/1122036.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... History of a Tragedy | | |\\n| BBC National Short Story Award | BBC National Short Story Award | | Ingrid Persaud | | | |\\n| Bookseller/Diagram Prize for Oddest Title of the Year | Bookseller/Diagram Prize for Oddest Title of the Year | | Achse Verlag | | | |\\n| Booker Prize | Booker Prize | | Anna Burns | Milkman | | |\\n| Booker Prize | International Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_in_literature\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"0b55466eaa655ac5c86685ecca30535c21ade307d9a3c9bab622184371089dac\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"8bd47ed75fb5c1f824de511923a5e3032d730e0cb3c66da699d94a43d6fc0f15\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Ismail Kadare Man Booker International Prize winner\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_2c5e1bd0c82c446b8d9190f5"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (2000s). Let me think about the 2010s winners and the \"translated into 25+ languages\" clue.\n\nLet me look at the International Booker Prize Wikipedia page to understand the timeline and winners, and also consider the DSC Prize for South Asian Literature (created 2010).","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d11\", \"goal\": \"International Booker Prize history winners 2005 2010s\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_7e5018426bc3454c89727312","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"DSC Prize South Asian Literature created 2010 winner\", \"novel translated 26 languages DSC Prize shortlist\", \"Jhumpa Lahiri translated 25 languages prize\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_decce22261b94facb5eaa55d","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d11\",\"document_chars\":27249,\"end\":26993,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"929b0e4b40f9a98330736c3b4fe3c125939ffa5b61388671abffeda41ec0fac6\",\"snapshot\":\"25e42c9d9629a06063929aefe4e8f050cac2c095d797b7476410c1a6fe277c5a\",\"start\":23993,\"text\":\"In addition, previous winners of the prize are automatically considered if they enter new titles. Books may also be called in: publishers can make written representations to the judges to consider titles in addition to those already entered. In the 21st century the average number of books considered by the judges has been approximately 130.\\n\\nRelated awards for translated works\\n\\nA separate prize for which any living writer in the world may qualify, the Man Booker International Prize, was inaugurated in 2005. Until 2015, it was given every two years to a living author of any nationality for a body of work published in English or generally available in English translation. In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now given annually to a single book in English translation, with a £50,000 prize for the winning title, shared equally between author and translator. The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ended its association with the prizes in 2019.\\n\\nA Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian writer, either written in English or translated into English, and published in the previous calendar year.\\n\\nFor many years, as part of The Times Literature Festival in Cheltenham, a Booker event was held on the last Saturday of the festival. Four guest speakers/judges debated a shortlist of four books from a given year from before the introduction of the Booker Prize, and a winner was chosen. Unlike the real Booker Prize (1969 through 2014), writers from outside the Commonwealth were also considered. In 2008, the winner for 1948 was Alan Paton's Cry, the Beloved Country, beating Norman Mailer's The Naked and the Dead, Graham Greene's The Heart of the Matter and Evelyn Waugh's The Loved One. In 2015, the winner for 1915 was Ford Madox Ford's The Good Soldier, beating The Thirty-Nine Steps (John Buchan), Of Human Bondage (W. Somerset Maugham), Psmith, Journalist (P. G. Wodehouse) and The Voyage Out (Virginia Woolf).Haslam, Sara (13 October 2015), \\\"Ford's The Good Soldier Wins The Cheltenham Booker 1915 at 2015 Festival\\\". Ford Madox Oxford Society. Retrieved 27 November 2016.\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* Baillie Gifford Prize (formerly the Samuel Johnson Prize)\\n* Commonwealth Writers Prize\\n* Costa Book Awards\\n* German Book Prize (Deutscher Buchpreis)\\n* Giller Prize (known as the Scotiabank Giller Prize from 2005 to 2023)\\n* Governor General's Awards\\n* Grand Prix of Literary Associations\\n* Miles Franklin Award\\n* Prix Goncourt\\n* Russian Booker Prize\\n* List of British literary awards\\n* List of literary awards\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nFurther reading\\n\\n* \\n* \\n* \\n\\nExternal links\\n\\n* (The Booker Prize)\\n* (Booker Prize Foundation)\\n* The Booker Prize Archive at Oxford Brookes University\\n* A primer on the Man Booker Prize and crit\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":26993,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false,\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":26993,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"international\",\"booker\",\"prize\",\"2005\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":6.753922,\"selected_block\":[24337,25007],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":23993},\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_7e5018426bc3454c89727312"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":false,\"blocks_finish\":true,\"code\":\"read_only_tool_only\",\"executed\":false,\"message\":\"This decision permits only read; no automatic replacement\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_decce22261b94facb5eaa55d"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (2000s). Let me think about the 2010s winners and the \"translated into 25+ languages\" clue. The Man Asian Literary Prize was created in 2007. Let me look at the International Booker Prize Wikipedia page directly.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize Wikipedia winners 2016 2017 2018 2019\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 winner\", \"International Booker Prize shortlist translated 25 languages\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_96b4ce51d1ed4c8e86768c3e","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":26993,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":23993}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... of Seven Killings | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2016 | Paul Beatty | The Sellout | Satire | |\\n| 2017 | George Saunders | Lincoln in the Bardo | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2018 | Anna Burns | Milkman | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Bernardine Evaristo The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-09-26 |website ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... Goes Last (2015) (Winner of the 2015 Red Tentacle award)\\n* Hag-Seed (2016) (Longlisted for the 2017 Women Prize for Fiction)\\n* The Testaments (2019, joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize)\\\"Margaret Atwood announces sequel to The Handmaid's Tale\\\" . CBC News, November 28, 2018.\\n\\n;Short fiction collections ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2016 The Booker Prizes |url= |url-status=live |archive-url= |archive-date=6 February 2023 |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en}} | Longlist | Elizabeth Strout | My Name Is Lucy Barton | Viking | * Amanda Foreman (chair) * Jon Day * David Harsent * Olivia Williams * Abdulrazak Gurnah |\\n| 2017 |